So, a second ascention, also a slash-n-grab sort.  Having almost NO
luck with casters.

This one went rather easily, all things considered.  And I brought
some more juice for the ice machine at the demigod bar.  That's all
the /oCold in the DoD, not a single charge used.

An altar on lv 3 gave Mojo, and there were 2 !oHW, 2 ?oEW, a Blessed
MM, and a co-aligned altar in minetown.  A throne wish early on
provided +3 SDSM, and a dip (also on lv 3, I recall) provided a pair
of +3 GoP.  Lots of money laying about, and about 4 temples and an
assortment of strong pets let me give early and often (and
repeatedly).  There was a 0:3 WoW laying around in Mine's End, and I
wished up an AK quite early. Since I'm such a packrat, a BBoH is high
on my wish list, and since I'm a moron a B"oLS is also rather a high
priority.  I was thinking to collect some gems, to bump up the score,
but I only found about a quarter of a million points worth.  Maybe I
should have wished up 4 wishes worth of dilithium crystals, but I was
lazy.  I did have a 0:0 left at the end.

Got me a couple of MM's and wrote up a bunch of scrolls, and before
the quest, even, I was kitted out with a blessed fixed AK, Mojo, FB,
and a +7 SS and an AC in the -30's. Yeah, that's what I'm talking
about.

And there were 3 deaths.  A c corpse, A black D corpse, and a WoD
bearing something or other while I was IDing scrolls.  See why the
"oLS(es)?

The end game was really dull, although the valk quest artifact qand a
=oTC makes moving around quite a bit easier.  I didn't know, however,
that that particular dealie stops working after you've got the AoY,
though I should have guessed.  At the VS, or rather LAYING ON TOP OF
the VS, there was another 0:3 WoW, which I used for some B?oFH to bump
up the HP's a little, and a =oLev, which I hadn't found by that point.
 That's also where I got the last "oLS, my fourth.

I just can't seem to send a character with a good name to the Demigod
Bar.  ChristAlmighty and Dawg?  Jeeze.  Samurai's with names like
Yoshi and Wizards named Merlin seem to die with some immediacy. 
Depressing, really.

I'm going to work on Wizards and Priests next, or a monk, or
SOMETHING.

